    "body": "Maintainer refresh for the 14:43 review (head bbc36e1 → **19c8ab0**), no force-push.\n\n**Conflicts and fixes**\n1. `crates/ui/src/egui_app/mod.rs` - kept both test modules: `ribbon_icon_tests` (this PR) and `fresh_op_tests` (main), each behind its own `#[cfg(test)]`. (The old head also had a bare `mod tool_number_tests;` without `#[cfg(test)]` after a blank line; the resolution restores the attribute.)\n2. `crates/ui/tests/snapshots/egui_app.png`, `egui_app_light.png`, `egui_tool_editor.png` - regenerated with `UPDATE_SNAPSHOTS=1` (CWD `crates/ui`) on this branch merged with current `origin/main` (8b0d784), i.e. on the exact tree that lands. Compared against main's goldens: the only visual change is the glyphs on the ribbon's section doors (Milling 2D/3D, Drilling, Multi-axis) and the machine door.\n\n**How it was merged.** The branch takes main up to 06a194c (#293) plus #232's head ce73602 (the only post-06a194c change to the three snapshots), not the tip of main: #277/#285 change `.github/workflows/`, which our push token cannot write. `git merge-tree` of the new head with `origin/main` is clean, its result is byte-identical to the tested tree for the three snapshots, and no `.github` file changed on the branch.\n\n**Tests** (tree = this head merged with origin/main 8b0d784, CWD `crates/ui`)\n```\ncargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib                          : 272 passed, 0 failed, 2 ignored\ncargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings : clean\n```\n",
